UFCPS Level 2 — Futuristic Expansion Roadmap v1

0. Status

Architecture level: 2
Name: Distributed Swarm Intelligence
Position: built above UFCPS Level 1
Repository strategy: same repository, separate swarm/ subsystem
Current state: conceptual architecture + first protocol specifications
Target: experimental platform for distributed swarm intelligence

1. Vision

UFCPS Level 1 defines continuity of a process independently of the identity of its current carrier.

Level 2 extends this principle into a distributed environment in which:

intelligence is distributed across agents;

computational and physical resources are distributed across providers;

unresolved questions are preserved in a common process memory;

tasks are discovered by agents rather than centrally assigned;

resources are aggregated dynamically;

research can continue after individual agents or resources disappear;

the system can identify missing infrastructure;

agents can formulate proposals to researchers, resource providers, and investors;

verified computational contribution can be economically compensated;

the economic protocol itself can be researched by the swarm.

The long-term vision is:

A continuously operating distributed process capable of organizing intelligence, resources, memory, experimentation, and economic coordination across a swarm of heterogeneous participants.

Level 2 does not assume that this automatically produces AGI.

The hypothesis is that this architecture may provide a practical substrate on which distributed swarm intelligence can emerge and be experimentally evaluated.

2. Relationship to Level 1

Level 1 remains the semantic foundation.

