6. Layer C — Resource Aggregation

Objective

Turn many independent small contributions into usable pools.

Provider A  -> 2 GPU-hours
Provider B  -> 5 GPU-hours
Provider C  -> 1 GPU-hour
Provider D  -> 40 GPU-hours
                  |
                  v
             COMPUTE POOL
                  |
                  v
              UFCPS TASK

Goals

batch small contributions;

preserve individual attribution;

reduce transaction overhead;

improve reliability;

tolerate node disappearance;

create temporary resource clusters;

support dynamic scaling.

Key concept

The swarm consumes capability, not ownership.

7. Layer D — Unresolved Question Ledger

Objective

Create a persistent distributed memory of unfinished processes.

The ledger stores:

question;

context;

hypotheses;

constraints;

attempts;

agents;

resources;

negative results;

deadlocks;

contradictions;

evidence;

unresolved differences;

required capabilities;

current process state;

continuation conditions.

Core transitions

OPEN
  |
DISCOVERABLE
  |
ACTIVE
  |
PARTIAL
  |
+--------------------+
|                    |
RESOLVED          CONTINUE
|                    |
ARCHIVE            NEW STATE

Important property

A question remains a process resource even when its current carrier disappears.

8. Layer E — Task Prospect

Objective

Expose unresolved questions as opportunities that agents can evaluate.

A Task Prospect should show:

problem;

current frontier;

previous attempts;

expected information gain;

required capabilities;

required compute;

uncertainty;

potential reuse;

continuation potential;

economic conditions.

The system should avoid forcing one universal "importance score".

Agents may apply their own utility functions.

Discovery model

Agent capabilities
        |
        v
Question matching
        |
        v
Task Prospects
        |
        +--> accept
        +--> reject
        +--> watch
        +--> request resources
        +--> propose method
        +--> split

